course: dictionary
lesson: 11777
title: A word inside a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are made of two smaller words stuck together. Look inside the word to find clues. Beanstalk is bean and stalk. A stalk is the long, thin stem that holds up a plant. «Our bean plant grew a tall beanstalk that twisted up the cane.» The stem is the stalk, so a beanstalk is a tall bean stem.
explain: Context tells you more. «Jack climbed the beanstalk and found a castle in the clouds.» A normal plant does not reach the clouds, so this beanstalk must be a magic one from a story. The words around a word can change what it means in each sentence.
explain: Always check your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «Jack climbed the tall bean stem and found a castle in the clouds.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A beanstalk is the tall stem of a bean plant.
fact: Bean plants can climb up a pole or a string, twisting around it as they grow.
fact: In the fairy tale «Jack and the Beanstalk», a magic beanstalk grows up into the clouds.
fact: The word is made of two words: bean and stalk. A stalk is a plant's stem.
fact: In science, children grow bean plants to see how stems grow towards the light.
exercise: «Our bean seed grew into a beanstalk that twisted up the cane.» What is a beanstalk? | A pot used for growing seeds | A small leaf that falls off in autumn | A kind of bean you eat in soup | *The tall stem of a bean plant that climbs a pole
exercise: «Jack climbed the beanstalk and found a castle in the clouds.» Where does this beanstalk come from? | A garden shed | A shop | A school science lab | *A fairy tale
exercise: Find the two smaller words inside beanstalk. | bea and nstalk | be and anstalk | *bean and stalk | beans and talk
test: «The bean plant grew so fast that its beanstalk reached the top of the fence.» What is the beanstalk in this sentence? | A long piece of string | A bean in a packet | A fence post | *The tall stem of the bean plant
test: Lily says the beanstalk in the story is just a normal plant. Why is she wrong? | *It grows up into the clouds, which a normal plant never does | Because stories never have plants | Because beans are not plants | Because beanstalks are always made of metal
exam: «Fee-fi-fo-fum» the giant roared, as Jack climbed down the beanstalk. What does beanstalk mean here? | *A tall, magic plant stem from the fairy tale | A bean that you can eat | A rope tied to a tree | A ladder in a shed
